<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Assiniboine</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Nakoda, Assiniboin</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Assiniboine, or Nakoda, are a Siouan-speaking Indigenous people of the northern Great Plains, in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saskatchewan">Saskatchewan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberta">Alberta</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/montana">Montana</a> and North Dakota. Having separated from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yanktonai">Yanktonai</a> Dakota, they became close allies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cree">Cree</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fur-trade">fur trade</a> and in wars with the Blackfoot and Dakota. Today they live on reserves and reservations in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/assiniboine.jpg" alt="Assiniboine" width="320" height="444" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Karl Bodmer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Assiniboin_indians_0065v.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
